-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 17 (Offences against property), part 4:
--   Mischief            ss 425-440 (ss 429-434 repealed)
--   Criminal trespass   ss 441-462 (ss 443-446 and 454-458 repealed)
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (inputs/PC1871.txt). Section text copied mechanically.
--
-- Before reading:
--
-- * Four facts records: `Mischief Facts` (ss 425-440), `Criminal Trespass
--   Facts` (ss 441-452, 458A-460), `Found Armed Facts` (s 453) and
--   `Receptacle Facts` (ss 461-462).
-- * "Mischief" (s 425) and "house-breaking" (s 442) are this group's
--   definitions, read elsewhere; they are exported as `commits mischief` and
--   `commits house-breaking`.
-- * ss 449-451 turn on how ANOTHER offence is punishable; that is a flat leaf
--   here (the charge generator cannot evaluate a second offence's punishment
--   from one facts record), whose @desc names pc-general's readers of a
--   `Punishment` (fork P-9).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Chapter 17 - Offences against property: mischief`

§§ `The facts of one act of mischief`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 425-440 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Mischief Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the property`        IS A STRING  @desc The property affected, as it is to read in the charge - for example "the windscreen of motor car SBA 1234 X"
    `the owner`           IS A STRING  @desc The person to whom wrongful loss or damage was intended or known likely, as it is to read after "to"; leave blank if the public
    `the act`             IS A STRING  @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit, by" - for example "smashing it with a hammer"

    -- s 425
    `with intent to cause`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to cause wrongful loss or damage? (fault element, s 26C)
    `knowing that he is likely to cause`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or know that he was likely to cause it? (fault element, s 26D)
    `wrongful loss`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... wrongful loss (s 23)?
    damage                IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... damage?
    `to the public`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... to the public?
    `to any person`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... to any person? It need not be the owner of the property (Explanation 1); the property may be the accused's own, or jointly owned (Explanation 2, illustration (g)).
    `causes the destruction of any property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the destruction of any property?
    `causes any such change in any property, or in the situation thereof`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause a change in any property, or in where it is? Illustration (c): throwing a ring into a river.
    `as destroys or diminishes its value or utility, or affects it injuriously`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that change destroy or diminish its value or utility, or affect it injuriously?

    -- s 427
    `causes a disruption`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause a disruption? (s 427)
    `which he knows is likely to cause a disruption`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or did the accused know it was likely to cause one? Illustration (c): no actual disruption is needed. (s 427)
    `to the provision of any key service`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... to the provision of a key service - water, sewerage, drainage, gas, electricity, waste, mass media, telecommunications; emergency services; payments, banking and securities services; healthcare; food supply; public transport; or any other service critical to public health, stability, defence or security (s 427(2))?
    `to the performance of any duty or function of, or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... to the performance of a duty or function, or the exercise of a power, of the Government or a public agency (a statutory body, a department or Ministry, or an Organ of State) (s 427(2))? Illustrations (a), (b).

    -- s 428
    `by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the mischief committed by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless an animal? (s 428)

    -- ss 435-438
    `by fire or any explosive substance`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the mischief committed (or attempted) by fire or any explosive substance? (ss 435, 436, 438)
    `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, damage to any property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, that he would thereby cause damage to any property? (s 435)
    `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, the destruction of any building`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, that he would thereby destroy a building? (s 436)
    `which is ordinarily used as a place for worship, for the administration of justice, for the transaction of public affairs, for education, or art, for public use or ornament, as a human dwelling, or as a place for the custody of property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that building ordinarily used for worship, the administration of justice, public affairs, education, art, public use or ornament, as a human dwelling, or for the custody of property? (s 436)
    `to any decked vessel`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the mischief committed to a decked vessel? (s 437)
    `to any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or to a vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards? Decide the burden with `20 tons or upwards`. (s 437)
    `intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe, that vessel`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend, or know it likely, that he would thereby destroy that vessel or render it unsafe? (s 437)
    `attempts to commit such mischief`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt (s 511, pc-general-part) to commit the mischief described in s 437? (s 438)

    -- s 439
    `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intentionally run a vessel aground or ashore? (s 439)
    `intending to commit theft of any property contained therein or to dishonestly misappropriate any such property, or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do so intending to commit theft of, or dishonestly misappropriate, property in the vessel, or intending that someone should? (s 439)

    -- s 440
    `having made preparation for causing to any person death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the accused made preparation for causing any person death, hurt (s 319) or wrongful restraint (s 339) - both pc-body-a's - or fear of any of them? (s 440)

§§ `s 425 - mischief`

-- 425. Whoever, with intent to cause, or knowing that he is likely to cause, wrongful
-- loss or damage to the public or any person, causes the destruction of any property, or any
-- such change in any property, or in the situation thereof, as destroys or diminishes its
-- value or utility, or affects it injuriously, commits "mischief".
--
-- Explanation 1.-It is not essential to the offence of mischief that the offender should intend to cause
-- loss or damage to the owner of the property injured or destroyed. It is sufficient if he intends to cause, or
-- knows that he is likely to cause, wrongful loss or damage to any person by injuring any property,
-- whether it belongs to that person or not.
--
-- Explanation 2.-Mischief may be committed by an act affecting property belonging to the person
-- who commits the act, or to that person and others jointly.
--
-- Illustrations
--
-- (a) A voluntarily burns a valuable security belonging to Z, intending to cause wrongful loss to Z. A
-- has committed mischief.
--
-- (b) [Deleted by Act 51 of 2007]
--
-- (c) A voluntarily throws into a river a ring belonging to Z, with the intention of thereby causing
-- wrongful loss to Z. A has committed mischief.
--
-- (d) A, knowing that his effects are about to be taken in execution, or under or pursuant to an
-- enforcement order, in order to satisfy a debt due from him to Z, destroys those effects, with the intention
-- of thereby preventing Z from obtaining satisfaction of the debt, and of thus causing damage to Z. A has
-- committed mischief.
--
-- (e) A, having insured a ship, voluntarily causes the same to be cast away, with the intention of
-- causing damage to the underwriters. A has committed mischief.
--
-- (f) A causes a ship to be cast away, intending thereby to cause damage to Z, who has lent money on
-- bottomry on the ship. A has committed mischief.
--
-- (g) A, having joint property with Z in a horse, shoots the horse, intending thereby to cause wrongful
-- loss to Z. A has committed mischief.
--
-- [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
@export Whether the accused "commits mischief" within section 425 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc What was done to the property, and with what intent or knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits mischief` f IF
        "Whoever,"
   ...  (    f's `with intent to cause`
        OR   f's `knowing that he is likely to cause` )
   ...  (    f's `wrongful loss`
        OR   f's damage )
   ...  (    f's `to the public`
        OR   f's `to any person` )
   ...  (    f's `causes the destruction of any property`
        OR   (    f's `causes any such change in any property, or in the situation thereof`
             AND  f's `as destroys or diminishes its value or utility, or affects it injuriously` ) )
   ...  ", commits mischief"

§§ `s 426 - punishment for committing mischief`

-- 426. Whoever commits mischief shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
-- which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- Punishment for committing mischief causing disruption to key service, etc.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 426
`punishment prescribed by s 426` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "426"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 426 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 426` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f

§§ `s 427 - punishment for committing mischief causing disruption to key service, etc.`

-- 427.-(1) Whoever commits mischief by doing any act which causes, or which he
-- knows is likely to cause, a disruption to -
--
-- (a) the provision of any key service; or
--
-- (b) the performance of any duty or function of, or the exercise of any power by
-- the Government or a public agency,
--
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (2) In subsection (1) -
--
-- "key service" means any of the following services:
--
-- (a) a service directly related to the provision to the general public of
-- water, sewerage, drainage, gas, electricity, waste collection and
-- disposal, newspapers, broadcasting, telecommunications and other
-- traditional forms of mass media communication (including radio and
-- television services);
--
-- (b) a search and rescue service, a fire-fighting service, a service
-- providing rapid response to requests for help in a medical emergency,
-- or other health emergency service;
--
-- (c) a payments clearing and settlement service for payment obligations or
-- securities, a service directly related to the provision to the general
-- public of banking facilities and financial services associated with
-- banking business, a securities trading, clearing and settlement service,
-- and any other like service that is necessary to the financial market or
-- financial institutions in Singapore or the disruption of which would
-- have a widespread adverse effect on the financial system in Singapore
-- or the economy of Singapore, or both;
--
-- (d) a service directly related to the provision to the general public of
-- health or healthcare services at a hospital, primary care healthcare
-- establishment or other like institution;
--
-- (e) a service that is critical to ensuring the reliable supply in Singapore of
-- food which is safe and suitable for human consumption;
--
-- (f) a service directly related to ensuring the provision to the general
-- public of reliable and safe public transport by land, water or air
-- within Singapore or to and from Singapore;
--
-- (g) any other service that is critical to maintaining public health, the
-- social and economic stability of Singapore or its people, or the
-- defence of Singapore or its national security;
--
-- "public agency" means -
--
-- (a) a body corporate or unincorporate established by or under any public
-- Act to perform or discharge a public function, or any part of such a
-- body; or
--
-- (b) a department or Ministry of the Government or an Organ of State.
--
-- Illustrations
--
-- (a) An act which causes damage to enforcement cameras installed in a public
-- place by a statutory board responsible for land transport to detect illegal parking
-- in a public road is an act which causes disruption to the performance of the
-- function of that statutory board.
--
-- (b) Unauthorised destruction of the records and files of a department of the
--
-- Government which role is to promote Singapore as a sound and reputable
-- financial centre is an act which causes disruption to the performance of the
-- function of that department.
--
-- (c) An act of mischief which damages an electricity licensee's power
-- generation facility that is used to supply electricity to a public housing estate, is
-- an act which is likely to cause disruption to a key service even though there is no
-- actual disruption to that power supply.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 427
`punishment prescribed by s 427` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "427"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 427 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief causing disruption to a key service, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and what it disrupted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 427` f IF
        "(1) Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  "by doing any act which"
   ...  (    f's `causes a disruption`
        OR   f's `which he knows is likely to cause a disruption` )
   ...  (    f's `to the provision of any key service`
        OR   f's `to the performance of any duty or function of, or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency` )

§§ `s 428 - mischief by killing or maiming any animal`

-- 428. Whoever commits mischief by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless,
-- any animal shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years,
-- or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 428
`punishment prescribed by s 428` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "428"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 428 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by killing or maiming any animal)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and the animal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 428` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  f's `by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal`

