§§ `s 435 - mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to cause damage`

-- 435. Whoever commits mischief by fire or any explosive substance, intending to
-- cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, damage to any property, shall
-- be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
-- liable to fine.
--
-- Mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 435
`punishment prescribed by s 435` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "435"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 435 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to cause damage)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and the means
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 435` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  f's `by fire or any explosive substance`
   ...  f's `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, damage to any property`

§§ `s 436 - mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc.`

-- 436. Whoever commits mischief by fire or any explosive substance, intending to
-- cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, the destruction of any
-- building which is ordinarily used as a place for worship, or for the administration of
-- justice, or for the transaction of public affairs, or for education, or art, or for public use
--
-- or ornament, or as a human dwelling, or as a place for the custody of property, shall be
-- punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 436
`punishment prescribed by s 436` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "436"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 436 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the means, and the building
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 436` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  f's `by fire or any explosive substance`
   ...  f's `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, the destruction of any building`
   ...  f's `which is ordinarily used as a place for worship, for the administration of justice, for the transaction of public affairs, for education, or art, for public use or ornament, as a human dwelling, or as a place for the custody of property`

§§ `s 437 - mischief with intent to destroy or make unsafe a decked vessel or a vessel of 20 tons burden`

-- 437. Whoever commits mischief to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of
-- 20 tons or upwards, intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that
-- he will thereby destroy or render unsafe that vessel, shall be punished with imprisonment
-- for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 437
`punishment prescribed by s 437` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "437"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether a vessel's burden is "20 tons or upwards" (s 437 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN tons IS A NUMBER @desc The vessel's burden, in tons
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `20 tons or upwards` tons IF tons AT LEAST 20

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 437 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief with intent to destroy or make unsafe a decked vessel or a vessel of 20 tons burden)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and the vessel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 437` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  (    f's `to any decked vessel`
        OR   f's `to any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards` )
   ...  f's `intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe, that vessel`

§§ `s 438 - punishment for the mischief described in section 437 when committed by fire or any explosive substance`

-- 438. Whoever commits or attempts to commit by fire or any explosive substance,
-- such mischief as is described in section 437, shall be punished with imprisonment for
-- life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not
-- sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- Punishment for intentionally running vessel aground or ashore with intent to
-- commit theft, etc.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 438
`punishment prescribed by s 438` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "438"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 438 of the Penal Code 1871 (the mischief of section 437 committed or attempted by fire or explosive substance)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief or attempt, the vessel, and the means
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 438` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    `offence under s 437` f
        OR   (    f's `attempts to commit such mischief`
             AND  (    f's `to any decked vessel`
                  OR   f's `to any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards` )
             AND  f's `intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe, that vessel` ) )
   ...  f's `by fire or any explosive substance`

§§ `s 439 - punishment for intentionally running vessel aground or ashore with intent to commit theft, etc.`

-- 439. Whoever intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore, intending to commit
-- theft of any property contained therein or to dishonestly misappropriate any such
