    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 439 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentionally running a vessel aground or ashore with intent to commit theft, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The grounding, and its purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 439` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  f's `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore`
   ...  f's `intending to commit theft of any property contained therein or to dishonestly misappropriate any such property, or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed`

§§ `s 440 - mischief committed after preparation made for causing death or hurt`

-- 440. Whoever commits mischief, having made preparation for causing to any person
-- death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall
-- also be liable to fine.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 440
`punishment prescribed by s 440` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "440"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 440 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief committed after preparation made for causing death or hurt)
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and the preparation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 440` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits mischief` f
   ...  f's `having made preparation for causing to any person death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint`

§§ `The mischief charges`

GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the mischief` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit mischief ",
           (IF f's `with intent to cause` THEN "with intent to cause " ELSE "knowing that you were likely to cause "),
           (`joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's `wrongful loss`) "wrongful loss"), (`included if` (f's damage) "damage")))),
           " to ", (IF f's `the owner` EQUALS "" THEN "the public" ELSE f's `the owner`),
           ", by causing ",
           (IF f's `causes the destruction of any property` THEN "the destruction of " ELSE "such change in "),
           f's `the property`,
           (IF f's `causes the destruction of any property` THEN "" ELSE " as diminished its value or utility or affected it injuriously"),
           (IF f's `the act` EQUALS "" THEN "" ELSE ", to wit, by " APPEND f's `the act`)

GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of mischief not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to cause` OR f's `knowing that he is likely to cause`) "with intent to cause, or knowing that he is likely to cause"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `wrongful loss` OR f's damage) "wrongful loss or damage"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `to the public` OR f's `to any person`) "to the public or any person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `causes the destruction of any property` OR (f's `causes any such change in any property, or in the situation thereof` AND f's `as destroys or diminishes its value or utility, or affects it injuriously`)) "causes the destruction of any property, or such change in it or its situation as destroys or diminishes its value or utility, or affects it injuriously"))

@export Frame a charge under section 426 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 426` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "426" "mischief"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 426`'s words)
        (`offence under s 426` f)
        (`the recital of the mischief` f)
        (`elements of mischief not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 427 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief causing disruption to key service, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the disruption, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 427` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "427(1)" "mischief causing disruption to key service, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 427`'s words)
        (`offence under s 427` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", which act ",
                (IF f's `causes a disruption` THEN "caused" ELSE "you knew was likely to cause"),
                " a disruption to ",
                (IF f's `to the provision of any key service` THEN "the provision of a key service" ELSE "the performance of a duty or function of the Government or a public agency"))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `causes a disruption` OR f's `which he knows is likely to cause a disruption`) "by doing any act which causes, or which he knows is likely to cause, a disruption"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `to the provision of any key service` OR f's `to the performance of any duty or function of, or the exercise of any power by the Government or a public agency`) "to the provision of a key service, or to the performance of a duty or function of the Government or a public agency")))

@export Frame a charge under section 428 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by killing or maiming any animal), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the animal, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 428` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "428" "mischief by killing or maiming any animal"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 428`'s words)
        (`offence under s 428` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless an animal")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal`) "by killing, poisoning, maiming or rendering useless any animal")))

@export Frame a charge under section 435 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to cause damage), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the means, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 435` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "435" "mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to cause damage"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 435`'s words)
        (`offence under s 435` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", by fire or an explosive substance, intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, damage to property")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `by fire or any explosive substance`) "by fire or any explosive substance"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, damage to any property`) "intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, damage to any property")))

@export Frame a charge under section 436 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the building, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 436` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "436" "mischief by fire or explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 436`'s words)
        (`offence under s 436` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", by fire or an explosive substance, intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause, the destruction of a building ordinarily used as a place of the kind described in section 436")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `by fire or any explosive substance`) "by fire or any explosive substance"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, the destruction of any building`) "intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause, the destruction of any building"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `which is ordinarily used as a place for worship, for the administration of justice, for the transaction of public affairs, for education, or art, for public use or ornament, as a human dwelling, or as a place for the custody of property`) "a building ordinarily used for worship, justice, public affairs, education, art, public use or ornament, as a human dwelling, or for the custody of property")))

GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`missing the vessel of section 437` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `to any decked vessel` OR f's `to any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards`) "to any decked vessel or any vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe, that vessel`) "intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby destroy or render unsafe, that vessel"))

@export Frame a charge under section 437 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief with intent to destroy or make unsafe a decked vessel or a vessel of 20 tons burden), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the vessel, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 437` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "437" "mischief with intent to destroy or make unsafe a decked vessel or a vessel of 20 tons burden"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 437`'s words)
        (`offence under s 437` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", being a decked vessel or a vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards, intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby destroy or render unsafe, the said vessel")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f), (`missing the vessel of section 437` f)))

@export Frame a charge under section 438 of the Penal Code 1871 (the mischief of section 437 committed by fire or explosive substance), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief or attempt, the vessel, the means, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 438` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "438" "mischief described in section 437 committed by fire or any explosive substance"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 438`'s words)
        (`offence under s 438` f)
        (CONCAT (IF `offence under s 437` f THEN "did commit" ELSE "did attempt to commit"),
                ", by fire or an explosive substance, mischief to ", f's `the property`,
                ", being a decked vessel or a vessel of a burden of 20 tons or upwards, intending to destroy or render unsafe, or knowing it to be likely that you would thereby destroy or render unsafe, the said vessel")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (`commits mischief` f OR f's `attempts to commit such mischief`) "commits or attempts to commit mischief"),
            (`missing the vessel of section 437` f),
            (`missing unless` (f's `by fire or any explosive substance`) "by fire or any explosive substance")))

@export Frame a charge under section 439 of the Penal Code 1871 (intentionally running vessel aground or ashore with intent to commit theft, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The grounding, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 439` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "439" "intentionally running vessel aground or ashore with intent to commit theft, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 439`'s words)
        (`offence under s 439` f)
        (CONCAT "did intentionally run a vessel, to wit, ", f's `the property`,
                ", aground or ashore, intending to commit theft of property contained therein or to dishonestly misappropriate such property, or with intent that such theft or misappropriation might be committed")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore`) "intentionally runs any vessel aground or ashore"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending to commit theft of any property contained therein or to dishonestly misappropriate any such property, or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed`) "intending to commit theft of, or dishonestly misappropriate, property contained therein, or with intent that such theft or misappropriation may be committed")))

@export Frame a charge under section 440 of the Penal Code 1871 (mischief committed after preparation made for causing death or hurt), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Mischief Facts` @desc The mischief, the preparation, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 440` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "440" "mischief committed after preparation made for causing death or hurt"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 440`'s words)
        (`offence under s 440` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the mischief` f), ", having made preparation for causing to any person death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of mischief not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `having made preparation for causing to any person death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint`) "having made preparation for causing to any person death or hurt or wrongful restraint, or fear of death or of hurt or of wrongful restraint")))

§ `Chapter 17 - Offences against property: criminal trespass`

§§ `The facts of one trespass`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 441-452, 458A-460 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Criminal Trespass Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the premises`        IS A STRING  @desc The property entered or remained in, as it is to read after "into" - for example "the flat at Blk 118 Bishan Street 12 #05-233"
    `the person in possession`
                          IS A STRING  @desc The person in possession of it, as it is to read after "in the possession of" - for example "one Ong Bee Choo"
    `the intended offence`
                          IS A STRING  @desc The offence the accused intended to commit, as it is to read after "with intent to commit" - for example "theft"; leave blank if the intent was to intimidate, insult or annoy

    -- s 441
    `enters into or upon property in the possession of another`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused enter into or upon property in another person's possession? Introducing any part of the body is entering (s 442 Explanation).
    `having lawfully entered into or upon such property, unlawfully remains there`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having entered lawfully, did the accused unlawfully remain there?
    `with intent to commit an offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused enter or remain with intent to commit an offence (s 40)?
    `with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy a person in possession of the property?

    -- s 442
    `any building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the place a building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling? (s 442)
    `any building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or a building used as a place for worship or for the custody of property? (s 442)

    -- ss 449-451
    `in order to commit any offence punishable with death`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the house-breaking committed in order to commit an offence punishable with death? (s 449) - read from that offence's `Punishment` with pc-general's `punishable with death or imprisonment for life`
    `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment for life`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life? (s 450)
    `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment? (s 451) - pc-general's `punishable with imprisonment`

    -- s 452
    `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person, or for assaulting any person, or for wrongfully restraining any person, or for putting any person in fear of hurt or of assault, or of wrongful restraint`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the accused made preparation for causing hurt, assaulting, wrongfully restraining, or putting in fear of hurt, assault or wrongful restraint, any person (ss 319, 351, 339 - pc-body-a's)? (s 452)

    -- s 458A
    `having been convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the accused already been convicted of an offence under s 449, 450, 451 or 452? (s 458A)

    -- s 459
    `causes grievous hurt to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc While committing the house-breaking, did the accused cause grievous hurt (s 320, pc-body-a) to any person? (s 459)
    `attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or attempt to cause death or grievous hurt to any person? (s 459)

    -- s 460
    `any person guilty of such house-breaking voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the house-breaking, did any person guilty of it voluntarily cause, or attempt to cause, death or grievous hurt to any person? (s 460)
    `jointly concerned in committing such house-breaking`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused jointly concerned in committing that house-breaking? (s 460)

§§ `s 441 - criminal trespass`

-- 441. Whoever enters into or upon property in the possession of another with intent to
-- commit an offence or to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such
-- property, or having lawfully entered into or upon such property, unlawfully remains
--
-- there with intent thereby to intimidate, insult or annoy any such person, or with intent to
-- commit an offence, is said to commit "criminal trespass".
@export Whether the accused "commits criminal trespass" within section 441 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The entry or remaining, and the intent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits criminal trespass` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    (    f's `enters into or upon property in the possession of another`
             AND  (    f's `with intent to commit an offence`
                  OR   f's `with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property` ) )
        OR   (    f's `having lawfully entered into or upon such property, unlawfully remains there`
             AND  (    f's `with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property`
                  OR   f's `with intent to commit an offence` ) ) )
   ...  ", is said to commit criminal trespass"

§§ `s 442 - house-breaking`

-- 442. Whoever commits criminal trespass by entering into, or remaining in, any
-- building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling, or any building used as a
-- place for worship or as a place for the custody of property, is said to commit
-- "house-breaking".
--
-- Explanation.-The introduction of any part of the criminal trespasser's body is entering sufficient to
-- constitute house-breaking.
--
-- [15/2019]
@export Whether the accused "commits house-breaking" within section 442 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The trespass, and the place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits house-breaking` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits criminal trespass` f
   ...  "by entering into, or remaining in,"
   ...  (    f's `any building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling`
        OR   f's `any building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property` )
   ...  ", is said to commit house-breaking"

-- s 443. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 444. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 445. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 446. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

§§ `s 447 - punishment for criminal trespass`

-- 447. Whoever commits criminal trespass shall be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with
-- both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 447
`punishment prescribed by s 447` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "447"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 447 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal trespass)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The trespass
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 447` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits criminal trespass` f

§§ `s 448 - punishment for house-breaking`

-- 448. Whoever commits house-breaking shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 448
`punishment prescribed by s 448` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "448"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 448 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 448` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f

§§ `s 449 - house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death`

-- 449. Whoever commits house-breaking in order to commit any offence punishable
-- with death, shall be punished with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 15 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life,
-- also be liable to fine.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 449
`punishment prescribed by s 449` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "449"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15 years, and shall, if he is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 449 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and its purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 449` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f
   ...  f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with death`

§§ `s 450 - house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life`

-- 450. Whoever commits house-breaking in order to commit any offence punishable
-- with imprisonment for life, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
