    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 450 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and its purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 450` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f
   ...  f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment for life`

§§ `s 451 - house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment`

-- 451. Whoever commits house-breaking in order to commit any offence punishable
-- with imprisonment, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- House-breaking after preparation made for causing hurt, etc.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 451
`punishment prescribed by s 451` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "451"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 451 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and its purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 451` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f
   ...  f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment`

§§ `s 452 - house-breaking after preparation made for causing hurt, etc.`

-- 452. Whoever commits house-breaking, having made preparation for causing hurt to
-- any person, or for assaulting any person, or for wrongfully restraining any person, or for
-- putting any person in fear of hurt or of assault, or of wrongful restraint, shall be punished
-- with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to
-- fine, or to caning.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 452
`punishment prescribed by s 452` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "452"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine, or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 452 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking after preparation made for causing hurt, etc.)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and the preparation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 452` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f
   ...  f's `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person, or for assaulting any person, or for wrongfully restraining any person, or for putting any person in fear of hurt or of assault, or of wrongful restraint`

§§ `s 453 - possession of house-breaking implements or offensive weapons`

-- 453.-(1) Any person who is found -
--
-- (a) armed with any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any
-- instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death,
-- without lawful authority or a lawful purpose;
--
-- (b) having his face covered or otherwise found disguised with intent to commit
-- any offence; or
--
-- (c) equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in
-- connection with any house-breaking,
--
-- shall be guilty of an offence and shall on conviction be punished with imprisonment for a
-- term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both; and any instrument or
-- article, mentioned in paragraph (a) or (c), found in the possession of that person shall be
-- forfeited.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (2) In any prosecution for an offence under subsection (1)(a), it is sufficient for the
-- prosecution to allege and prove that the accused was found to be armed with any
-- instrument mentioned in paragraph (a) and the burden is then on the accused to show
-- that he had lawful authority or a lawful purpose to be so armed.
--
-- [15/2019]
--
-- (3) An article or instrument is presumed to be carried with lawful authority if it is
-- carried by -
--
-- (a) any member of the Singapore Armed Forces, the Singapore Police Force,
-- the Singapore Civil Defence Force or any auxiliary police force created
-- under any written law;
--
-- (b) a forensic specialist or law enforcement officer acting in the course of his
-- duty as such in accordance with the Police Force Act 2004;
--
-- [Act 43 of 2024 wef 24/03/2025]
--
-- (c) any visiting force lawfully present in Singapore under the provisions of
-- any law relating to visiting forces; or
--
-- (d) any person as part of his official or ceremonial dress on any official or
-- ceremonial occasion.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 453
`punishment prescribed by s 453` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "453"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both; and any instrument or article, mentioned in paragraph (a) or (c), found in the possession of that person shall be forfeited"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `shall be punished with`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 453 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Found Armed Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the accused was found
    `the article`         IS A STRING  @desc The instrument, article or disguise, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a chopper about 30 cm long"
    `found armed with any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Was the accused found armed with an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or one likely to cause death if used as a weapon of offence?
    `with lawful authority or a lawful purpose`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused shown that he had lawful authority or a lawful purpose to be so armed? The burden is on the accused once the arming is proved (s 453(2)).
    `carried by a person listed in section 453(3)`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it carried by a member of the SAF, SPF, SCDF or an auxiliary police force; a forensic specialist or law enforcement officer on duty under the Police Force Act 2004; a lawfully present visiting force; or a person as part of official or ceremonial dress on an official or ceremonial occasion? If so it is presumed carried with lawful authority (s 453(3)).
    `having his face covered or otherwise found disguised`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Was the accused found with his face covered, or otherwise disguised?
    `with intent to commit any offence`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... with intent to commit an offence? (b)
    `equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Was the accused found equipped with an article or instrument for use in or in connection with house-breaking (s 442)?

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 453 of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of house-breaking implements or offensive weapons)
GIVEN f IS A `Found Armed Facts` @desc What the accused was found with, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 453` f IF
        "(1) Any person who is found -"
   ...  (    (    "(a)"
             AND  f's `found armed with any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death`
             AND  "without lawful authority or a lawful purpose"
             AND  NOT f's `with lawful authority or a lawful purpose`
             AND  "(3) presumed carried with lawful authority if carried by"
             AND  NOT f's `carried by a person listed in section 453(3)` )
        OR   (    "(b)"
             AND  f's `having his face covered or otherwise found disguised`
             AND  f's `with intent to commit any offence` )
        OR   (    "(c)"
             AND  f's `equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking` ) )

@export Frame a charge under section 453 of the Penal Code 1871 (possession of house-breaking implements or offensive weapons), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Found Armed Facts` @desc What the accused was found with, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 453` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "453(1)" "possession of house-breaking implements or offensive weapons"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 453`'s words)
        (`offence under s 453` f)
        (CONCAT "were found ",
                (`joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
                    (`included if` (f's `found armed with any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death` AND (NOT f's `with lawful authority or a lawful purpose`) AND (NOT f's `carried by a person listed in section 453(3)`)) "armed with an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, without lawful authority or a lawful purpose"),
                    (`included if` (f's `having his face covered or otherwise found disguised` AND f's `with intent to commit any offence`) "having your face covered or otherwise disguised with intent to commit an offence"),
                    (`included if` (f's `equipped with any article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with any house-breaking`) "equipped with an article or instrument for use in the course of or in connection with house-breaking")))),
                ", to wit, ", f's `the article`)
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 453` f) "found armed without lawful authority or a lawful purpose (section 453(1)(a)), or disguised with intent to commit an offence ((b)), or equipped for house-breaking ((c))")

-- s 454. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 455. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 456. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 457. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]
-- s 458. [Repealed by Act 15 of 2019]

§§ `s 458A - punishment for subsequent offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452`

-- 458A. Whoever, having been convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or
-- 452, commits an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452 shall be liable to caning in
-- addition to the punishment prescribed for that offence.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 458A
`punishment prescribed by s 458A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "458A"
    words                    IS "caning in addition to the punishment prescribed for that offence"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 458A of the Penal Code 1871 (a subsequent offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and the accused's record
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 458A` f IF
        "Whoever,"
   ...  f's `having been convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452`
   ...  ", commits an offence under section"
   ...  (    `offence under s 449` f
        OR   `offence under s 450` f
        OR   `offence under s 451` f
        OR   `offence under s 452` f )

§§ `s 459 - grievous hurt caused while committing house-breaking`

-- 459. Whoever, while committing house-breaking, causes grievous hurt to any person,
-- or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person, shall be punished with
-- imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 20 years and with
-- caning.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 459
`punishment prescribed by s 459` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "459"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 20 years and with caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall be punished with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 459 of the Penal Code 1871 (grievous hurt caused while committing house-breaking)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and the harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 459` f IF
        "Whoever, while"
   ...  `commits house-breaking` f
   ...  (    f's `causes grievous hurt to any person`
        OR   f's `attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person` )

§§ `s 460 - house-breaking when death or grievous hurt caused`

-- 460. If, at the time of the committing of house-breaking, any person guilty of such
-- offence voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person,
-- every person jointly concerned in committing such house-breaking, shall be punished
--
-- with imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 20 years.
--
-- [15/2019]
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 460
`punishment prescribed by s 460` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "460"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term of not less than 3 years and not more than 20 years"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 460 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking when death or grievous hurt caused)
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, the harm, and the accused's part
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 460` f IF
        "If, at the time of the committing of house-breaking,"
   ...  f's `any person guilty of such house-breaking voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`
   ...  ", every person"
   ...  f's `jointly concerned in committing such house-breaking`

§§ `The criminal trespass charges`

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the intent` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to commit an offence`) (CONCAT "with intent to commit an offence", (IF f's `the intended offence` EQUALS "" THEN "" ELSE CONCAT ", to wit, ", f's `the intended offence`))),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property`) "with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy the person in possession of the said property")))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the trespass` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit criminal trespass by ",
           (IF f's `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` THEN "entering into " ELSE "unlawfully remaining in "),
           f's `the premises`, ", in the possession of ", f's `the person in possession`, ", ", (`the intent` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the house-breaking` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did commit house-breaking by ",
           (IF f's `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` THEN "entering into " ELSE "unlawfully remaining in "),
           f's `the premises`, ", ",
           (IF f's `any building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling` THEN "used as a human dwelling" ELSE "a building used as a place for worship or for the custody of property"),
           ", in the possession of ", f's `the person in possession`, ", ", (`the intent` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of criminal trespass not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `enters into or upon property in the possession of another` OR f's `having lawfully entered into or upon such property, unlawfully remains there`) "enters into or upon property in the possession of another, or having lawfully entered, unlawfully remains there"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `with intent to commit an offence` OR f's `with intent to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property`) "with intent to commit an offence or to intimidate, insult or annoy any person in possession of such property"))

GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of house-breaking not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST (`elements of criminal trespass not made out` f),
                 (`missing unless` (f's `any building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling` OR f's `any building used as a place for worship or as a place for the custody of property`) "any building, tent, container or vessel used as a human dwelling, or any building used as a place for worship or for the custody of property (section 442)"))

@export Frame a charge under section 447 of the Penal Code 1871 (criminal trespass), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The trespass, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 447` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "447" "criminal trespass"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 447`'s words)
        (`offence under s 447` f)
        (`the recital of the trespass` f)
        (`elements of criminal trespass not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 448 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 448` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "448" "house-breaking"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 448`'s words)
        (`offence under s 448` f)
        (`the recital of the house-breaking` f)
        (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 449 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, its purpose, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 449` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "449" "house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with death"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 449`'s words)
        (`offence under s 449` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", in order to commit an offence punishable with death")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with death`) "in order to commit any offence punishable with death")))

@export Frame a charge under section 450 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, its purpose, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 450` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "450" "house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 450`'s words)
        (`offence under s 450` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment for life")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment for life`) "in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment for life")))

@export Frame a charge under section 451 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, its purpose, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 451` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "451" "house-breaking in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 451`'s words)
        (`offence under s 451` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", in order to commit an offence punishable with imprisonment")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment`) "in order to commit any offence punishable with imprisonment")))

@export Frame a charge under section 452 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking after preparation made for causing hurt, etc.), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, the preparation, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 452` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "452" "house-breaking after preparation made for causing hurt, etc."
        (`punishment prescribed by s 452`'s words)
        (`offence under s 452` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", having made preparation for causing hurt to any person, or for assaulting or wrongfully restraining any person, or for putting any person in fear of hurt, assault or wrongful restraint")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `having made preparation for causing hurt to any person, or for assaulting any person, or for wrongfully restraining any person, or for putting any person in fear of hurt or of assault, or of wrongful restraint`) "having made preparation for causing hurt, assault or wrongful restraint, or fear of any of them, to any person")))

@export Frame a charge under section 458A of the Penal Code 1871 (a subsequent offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, the prior conviction, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 458A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge read with` (f's particulars)
        (BRANCH
            IF `offence under s 449` f THEN "449"
            IF `offence under s 450` f THEN "450"
            IF `offence under s 452` f THEN "452"
            OTHERWISE                       "451")
        (LIST "458A")
        "a subsequent offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 458A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 458A` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", having been previously convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `having been convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452`) "having been convicted of an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452"),
            (`missing unless` (`offence under s 449` f OR `offence under s 450` f OR `offence under s 451` f OR `offence under s 452` f) "commits an offence under section 449, 450, 451 or 452")))

@export Frame a charge under section 459 of the Penal Code 1871 (grievous hurt caused while committing house-breaking), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, the harm, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 459` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "459" "grievous hurt caused while committing house-breaking"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 459`'s words)
        (`offence under s 459` f)
        (CONCAT (`the recital of the house-breaking` f), ", and while committing the said house-breaking, did ",
                (IF f's `causes grievous hurt to any person` THEN "cause grievous hurt to a person" ELSE "attempt to cause death or grievous hurt to a person"))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of house-breaking not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `causes grievous hurt to any person` OR f's `attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`) "causes grievous hurt, or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt, to any person")))

@export Frame a charge under section 460 of the Penal Code 1871 (house-breaking when death or grievous hurt caused), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Criminal Trespass Facts` @desc The house-breaking, the harm, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 460` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "460" "house-breaking when death or grievous hurt caused"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 460`'s words)
        (`offence under s 460` f)
        (CONCAT "were jointly concerned in committing house-breaking into ", f's `the premises`,
                ", at the time of which a person guilty of the said house-breaking voluntarily caused or attempted to cause death or grievous hurt to a person")
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `any person guilty of such house-breaking voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person`) "any person guilty of such house-breaking voluntarily causes or attempts to cause death or grievous hurt to any person"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `jointly concerned in committing such house-breaking`) "jointly concerned in committing such house-breaking")))

§§ `ss 461-462 - dishonestly breaking open a closed receptacle`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 461, 462 - the operative atoms, and the particulars CPC s 124 requires
DECLARE `Receptacle Facts` HAS
    particulars           IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `the receptacle`      IS A STRING  @desc The receptacle, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a locked cash box belonging to one Lim Ah Seng"
    dishonestly           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act dishonestly (s 24)?
    `with intent to commit mischief`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... or with intent to commit mischief (s 425)?
    `breaks open or unfastens`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused break open or unfasten the receptacle?
    `any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a closed receptacle which contained, or which the accused believed to contain, property?
    `being entrusted with the receptacle`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the receptacle been entrusted to the accused? (s 462)
    `without having authority to open the same`
                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... without authority to open it? (s 462)

-- 461. Whoever dishonestly, or with intent to commit mischief, breaks open or
-- unfastens any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property,
-- shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with
-- fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 461
`punishment prescribed by s 461` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "461"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 461 of the Penal Code 1871 (dishonestly breaking open a closed receptacle containing or supposed to contain property)
GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts` @desc The receptacle, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 461` f IF
        "Whoever"
   ...  (    f's dishonestly
        OR   f's `with intent to commit mischief` )
   ...  f's `breaks open or unfastens`
   ...  f's `any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property`

-- 462. Whoever, being entrusted with any closed receptacle which contains or which he
-- believes to contain property, without having authority to open the same, dishonestly, or
-- with intent to commit mischief, breaks open or unfastens that receptacle, shall be
-- punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or
-- with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 462
`punishment prescribed by s 462` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "462"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 462 of the Penal Code 1871 (breaking open a closed receptacle by a person entrusted with its custody)
GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts` @desc The receptacle, the entrustment, and what the accused did to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 462` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
   ...  f's `being entrusted with the receptacle`
   ...  f's `without having authority to open the same`
   ...  `offence under s 461` f

GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the recital of the breaking open` f MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", (IF f's dishonestly THEN "dishonestly" ELSE "with intent to commit mischief"),
           " break open or unfasten a closed receptacle which contained or which you believed to contain property, to wit, ", f's `the receptacle`

GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of breaking open not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's dishonestly OR f's `with intent to commit mischief`) "dishonestly, or with intent to commit mischief"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `breaks open or unfastens`) "breaks open or unfastens"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property`) "any closed receptacle which contains or which he believes to contain property"))

@export Frame a charge under section 461 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts` @desc The receptacle, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 461` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "461" "dishonestly breaking open any closed receptacle containing or supposed to contain property"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 461`'s words)
        (`offence under s 461` f)
        (`the recital of the breaking open` f)
        (`elements of breaking open not made out` f)

@export Frame a charge under section 462 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Receptacle Facts` @desc The receptacle, the entrustment, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 462` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "462" "breaking open a closed receptacle by a person entrusted with its custody"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 462`'s words)
        (`offence under s 462` f)
        (CONCAT "being entrusted with a closed receptacle and without having authority to open the same, ", (`the recital of the breaking open` f))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `being entrusted with the receptacle`) "being entrusted with any closed receptacle"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `without having authority to open the same`) "without having authority to open the same"),
            (`elements of breaking open not made out` f)))
